      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A case study for reference:\n\nWhen a singer is performing on stage and they are streaming their audio performance through a video player, you still want them to look like they are singing, even though they are not transmitting sound through their normal microphone.\n\nCurrently with the 5% level, you hear the person in VR and then slightly delayed because of the streaming lag, so long as their voice hits the microphone threshold, and this is not ideal.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
