      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{695be2c3f85d59c66dc3f614|full_name} Seconding what Alto has to say here, as a frequent VRChat performer who streams audio into the world through VRCDN into a video player, I want people to be able to see my mouth moving, not only for the live performance, but also for recording my own performances.  Since my own headset doesn't support face tracking and a suitable solution still on the way, it would be nice for visemes to still be enabled even if I mute myself or turn my volume to 0%, as 5% is still quite audible to an audience.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
